<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>AST explorer</title>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="description" content="An online AST explorer.">
    <%= htmlWebpackPlugin.files.webpackManifest %>
    <!-- Repair-Bench offline adaptation. The seed loaded a third party analytics
         script from plausible.astexplorer.net here (website/index.ejs:8). That was the
         ONLY genuine cross origin subresource load on the runtime path of this face; the
         seven https anchors in the #contribution footer below and the two https anchors
         in the toolbar are <a href> documentation links, which pull nothing until they
         are activated, and no checkpoint activates one. The script is replaced by an
         inline same origin no-op that keeps window.plausible callable so a reference to
         it can never throw, and transfers zero bytes. No module under website/src reads
         window.plausible (grep at design time: 0 hits), so this stub cannot change any
         observed behaviour. The seven footer anchors are deliberately KEPT and are
         recorded as non egress in meta.external_face.census. -->
    <script>window.plausible = window.plausible || function () {};</script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="page">
      <div id="container"></div>
      <div id="contribution">
        Built with
        <a href="https://reactjs.org/">React</a>,
        <a href="https://babeljs.io/">Babel</a>,
        <a href="https://fontawesome.com/">Font Awesome</a>,
        <a href="https://codemirror.net/">CodeMirror</a>,
        <a href="https://expressjs.com/">Express</a>,
        and
        <a href="https://webpack.js.org/">webpack</a>
        |
        <a href="https://github.com/fkling/astexplorer">GitHub</a>
        |
        <span>@@COMMIT@@</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
